# Test: interface backend kernel refuses firewall backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse `firewall backend vpp` when
#           `interface backend` is `kernel` (by default), naming the leaf and
#           both fixes (`set firewall backend kernel` and `set interface
#           backend vpp`)?
#           A unit test cannot prove `ze config validate` evaluates the real
#           registered selectors against the loaded YANG schema.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-4 (firewall) -- mismatched
#            `firewall backend vpp` under kernel interfaces is refused with
#            both operator fixes.
# PREVENTS: VPP ACLs being configured on a kernel-forwarding router where no
#           VPP interfaces carry the traffic.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
firewall {
	backend vpp;
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=firewall backend
expect=stdout:contains=set firewall backend kernel
expect=stdout:contains=set interface backend vpp
